{"blocks":[["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2200","4. Drill into the buffer group",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2239","Press <Space>b.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","4. Drill into the buffer group"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2262","Notice: this list is generated live from my actually-open buffers, not hand-written.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","4. Drill into the buffer group"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2352","5. Drill into the windows group",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2392","Press <Space>w.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","5. Drill into the windows group"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2415","Notice: this group is a proxy for <C-w> — every entry is really a <C-w> command, generated live from my current window layout.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","5. Drill into the windows group"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2553","6. Trigger Window Hydra Mode directly",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2599","Press <C-w><Space> (control-w, then space) instead of going through the leader.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","6. Trigger Window Hydra Mode directly"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2686","Notice: the popup stays open across repeated presses — try a couple of the resize or focus keys — instead of closing after one keystroke. This is nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Hydra Mode; see LazyVim/Keyshort/Window/Split for the window commands it exposes. Press <Esc> to leave it.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","6. Trigger Window Hydra Mode directly"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-2985","7. Check the non-leader groups",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3024","Press g alone (not after leader) and pause: the goto group, with gs nesting further into surround.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","7. Check the non-leader groups"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3136","Press [ or ] alone and pause: prev/next groups.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","7. Check the non-leader groups"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3197","Press z alone and pause: the fold group.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","7. Check the non-leader groups"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3247","8. Find my own keymap in the popup",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3290","Press y alone and pause.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","8. Find my own keymap in the popup"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3322","Look for yp (yank current buffer path) in the list — it has a description but sits outside any named group.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","8. Find my own keymap in the popup"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3439","Notice: which-key doesn't need a group registration to show a keymap — any vim.keymap.set(..., { desc = \"...\" }) is enough on its own. Named groups only exist to label a prefix that multiple keys share.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Steps","8. Find my own keymap in the popup"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3653","Verification",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3672","<Space>? opens a popup scoped to the current buffer only.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Verification"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3736","<Space> alone (paused) opens a small, corner-anchored popup rather than a full-width list.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Verification"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3833","<Space>b and <Space>w reflect my actual open buffers and window layout, not a static list.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Verification"]],["nvim/Plugin/which-key.nvim/Tutorial/Navigate%20My%20Which-Key%20Menus/","source-block-3932","<C-w><Space> keeps its popup open across several keystrokes until <Esc>.",["Tutorial: Navigate My Which-Key Menus","Verification"]]],"format_version":5}